cates an action or state that is stable, quasi-permanent, likely to lastnote	GL 1.8, 4.1a, 4.61(7), 5.41, 6.41, 6.492; ult. from same etymon as t—a (V) 'place, put' [q.v.]; contrast \o (Pv) 'change of state'; t—a almost never occurs after Vadj's, since adjectives are already stative in meaning (a possible exception is the RL ex. given first below, where t—a follows y\ï (Vadj) 'be long')ex  	q\ø÷ thu ni l‰ y\ï t—a l»a qo y\a÷ ve t\‰ «s—î ve y\o exgl	[RL] When you span it again and find that it's long[er], you know that a sin has been committed.ex  	y\‰-m|î h»o÷ t—a «s—e exgl	Shut the door first.ex  	chø-m»ø chi t»e ni le-le y\‰-qhø t\e÷-ch|î m»a te-te l‰ ch»‰ t—a ve exgl	That old man sits in the house every day doing nothing.ex  	|a-qhø ch»‰ t—a ve chø \ø-po \a-th\o÷=ma v\ï t—a ve le exgl	What have you bought for the people who have stayed at home?note	note both occurrences of t—a, after ch»‰ (V) 'stay' and v\ï (V) 'buy'ngl 	2. (perfective) indicates an action or state that is prior to the moment of interest and relevant to it..hw 	c»ø t—a ve v\a÷=|o-q—opos 	LRC + Nhgl  	a pig's head that has been boiledex  	y»ø Ÿg»a÷-u l\ø t—a ve y\o exgl	He had already asked for chicken-eggs.ex  	≥\a ha-pa=«s|ï v»en-qhø q\ø÷ qay t\u d»ø t—a ve y\o exgl	I have decided to go into town again next month.ex  	»o ve —ø t»e Ÿg»a le-le «s—î t—a ve h|‰ exgl	Everybody probably knows that already.ex  	«sï t—a ve chï=p|î-qw\‰÷ qh\a-qhe ca p\‰ t\u ve le exgl	How shall we divide up the barking-deer which has died?ex  	≥\a t|a-p»o÷ l|ay m\a v\ï t—a ve y\o exgl	I have bought several bags..hw 	t—a-n—apos 	Advloan	LOANgl  	*really, *truly; *stronglynote	< Shan; prob. & \ø-t\‰-\ø-na (Elabadv)ex  	n\ø t—a-n—a «s—î qo ≥\a \a÷ tho m—a l»a c»ø q»o÷-ma exgl	If you really do understand, you ought to explain it to me!.hw 	t—a-n\u÷  ±  t\a÷-n\o÷bz  	[q.v.]pos 	Nloan	LOANgl  	*policenote	< Tai (cf. Si. tamr\uat), ult. < Khmer; the usual BL form is t\a÷-n\o÷ [q.v.]..